      "summaries": {
        "en": "TeslaMate is a self-hosted data logger for Tesla vehicles that automatically collects and visualizes driving data. It uses Elixir/Phoenix for the backend and Grafana for dashboards, storing data in PostgreSQL. Technically, it leverages MQTT for real-time telemetry and integrates with OpenStreetMap for route mapping. You can deploy it via Docker or Nix, and extend it with home automation systems. Ideal for owners who want detailed analytics, trip history, and battery stats without relying on Tesla's cloud.",
        "zh": "TeslaMate 是一款自托管的数据记录器，专为特斯拉车主设计，自动收集并可视化驾驶数据。它基于 Elixir/Phoenix 构建后端，使用 Grafana 展示仪表盘，数据存储在 PostgreSQL 中。技术亮点在于通过 MQTT 实现实时遥测，并集成 OpenStreetMap 进行路线映射。你可以通过 Docker 或 Nix 轻松部署，还能与家庭自动化系统联动。适合希望深度分析行程、电池状态和能耗的车主，完全掌控自己的数据，无需依赖特斯拉云端。",
        "es": "TeslaMate is a self-hosted data logger for Tesla vehicles that automatically collects and visualizes driving data. It uses Elixir/Phoenix for the backend and Grafana for dashboards, storing data in PostgreSQL. Technically, it leverages MQTT for real-time telemetry and integrates with OpenStreetMap for route mapping. You can deploy it via Docker or Nix, and extend it with home automation systems. Ideal for owners who want detailed analytics, trip history, and battery stats without relying on Tesla's cloud.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "teslamate stands out for dashboard, datalogger, and docker in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "TeslaMate is a self-hosted data logger for Tesla vehicles that automatically collects and visualizes driving data. It uses Elixir/Phoenix for the backend and Grafana for dashboards, storing data in PostgreSQL. Technically, it leverages MQTT for real-time telemetry and integrates with OpenStreetMap for route mapping. You can deploy it via Docker or Nix, and extend it with home automation systems. Ideal for owners who want detailed analytics, trip history, and battery stats without relying on Tesla's cloud.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/teslamate-org/teslamate for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
