      "summaries": {
        "en": "optimizerDuck is a free, open-source Windows optimization tool designed to boost performance, enhance privacy, and simplify system tweaking. It consolidates dozens of common registry and service adjustments into a clean interface, making it easy for gamers and power users to debloat Windows without manual scripting. You can run it directly from GitHub to disable telemetry, stop unnecessary services, or apply gaming-focused tweaks. Its modular design invites contributors to add new optimizations, and you can fork it to build custom presets for your own deployment needs.",
        "zh": "optimizerDuck 是一款免费开源的 Windows 优化工具，旨在提升系统性能、保护隐私并简化调优流程。它将数十种常见的注册表和服务调整整合到简洁的界面中，让游戏玩家和高级用户无需手动编写脚本即可轻松精简 Windows。你可以直接从 GitHub 运行它，禁用遥测、停止不必要的服务或应用游戏优化。其模块化设计鼓励贡献者添加新的优化项，你也可以 Fork 项目来构建自定义预设，满足个人或企业部署需求。",
        "es": "optimizerDuck is a free, open-source Windows optimization tool designed to boost performance, enhance privacy, and simplify system tweaking. It consolidates dozens of common registry and service adjustments into a clean interface, making it easy for gamers and power users to debloat Windows without manual scripting. You can run it directly from GitHub to disable telemetry, stop unnecessary services, or apply gaming-focused tweaks. Its modular design invites contributors to add new optimizations, and you can fork it to build custom presets for your own deployment needs.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "optimizerDuck stands out for csharp, debloat, and dotnet in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "optimizerDuck is a free, open-source Windows optimization tool designed to boost performance, enhance privacy, and simplify system tweaking. It consolidates dozens of common registry and service adjustments into a clean interface, making it easy for gamers and power users to debloat Windows without manual scripting. You can run it directly from GitHub to disable telemetry, stop unnecessary services, or apply gaming-focused tweaks. Its modular design invites contributors to add new optimizations, and you can fork it to build custom presets for your own deployment needs.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/itsfatduck/optimizerDuck for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
